1
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,380
The Hallam Nuclear Power Facility is located in the central United States near the town

2
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:37,019
of Hallam in the state of Nebraska.

3
00:00:37,019 --> 00:00:41,899
The most advanced utility nuclear power plant in the nation, it was built by the Atomic

4
00:00:41,899 --> 00:00:50,019
Energy Commission and the Consumers Public Power District of Nebraska.

5
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:55,240
TALEM is operated by consumers under the Atomic Energy Commission Power Demonstration Reactor

6
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:57,420
program.

7
00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:17,439
At 252,000 thermal kilowatts, its sodium graphite reactor produces 79,400 net kilowatts of electricity.

8
00:01:17,439 --> 00:01:23,159
The feasibility of the sodium-graphite concept was established by the Sodium Reactor Experiment

9
00:01:23,159 --> 00:01:29,700
built and operated since 1957 near Los Angeles, California by Atomics International for the

10
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:34,799
Atomic Energy Commission.

11
00:01:34,799 --> 00:01:40,379
As a result of experience gained from Sodium Reactor Experiment operation, Atomics International

12
00:01:40,379 --> 00:01:46,340
was assigned overall technical responsibility for the design of Hallam, the first central

13
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:50,740
station sodium graphite reactor plant.

14
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:59,659
The core of the Hallam reactor is contained in a stainless steel tank.

15
00:01:59,659 --> 00:02:05,420
Metallic uranium alloy fuel contained in clusters of stainless steel tubes is

16
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:11,719
suspended in the core. Stainless steel clad graphite moderator elements

17
00:02:11,719 --> 00:02:21,199
surround the fuel elements. Liquid sodium serves as the coolant and heat transfer

18
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:28,319
medium. From the bottom of the reactor vessel, the sodium flows up past the hot

19
00:02:28,319 --> 00:02:33,039
fuel elements to an upper pool, then out of the vessel at a temperature of

20
00:02:33,039 --> 00:02:41,859
approximately 950 degrees Fahrenheit. The primary sodium coolant becomes

21
00:02:41,859 --> 00:02:48,459
radioactive during its passage through the core. This radioactive sodium is

22
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:53,500
pumped through three identical primary loops to intermediate heat exchangers

23
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:59,219
and returned to the reactor vessel at approximately 600 degrees Fahrenheit to

24
00:02:59,219 --> 00:03:09,280
repeat the cycle. The heat carried by the sodium in the primary loop is transferred

25
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:14,400
by the intermediate heat exchangers to the three secondary sodium loops which

26
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:21,419
are non-radioactive. The heat from the secondary non-radioactive loops is fed

27
00:03:21,419 --> 00:03:26,919
to three steam generators producing steam to turn the conventional turbine

28
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:37,540
generator. In January 1962, the reactor was placed in operation for the first

29
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:46,020
time in dry critical low-power tests. Wet critical and low-power tests were

30
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:55,060
started in August 1962. Reliability of the control and safety equipment was

31
00:03:55,060 --> 00:04:03,640
determined and verified with each increase in power. In May 1963 electricity

32
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:07,400
produced by the Hallam nuclear power facility began flowing through power

33
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:20,199
lines. Operation of the nuclear plant has been smooth responsive and reliable. The

34
00:04:20,199 --> 00:04:27,959
plant follows load automatically. Outstanding heat transfer characteristics of sodium coolant

35
00:04:27,959 --> 00:04:32,759
make the sodium graphite concept particularly suitable to follow rapid load swings.

36
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:42,039
Steam turbine inlet conditions of 850 degrees Fahrenheit and 850 PSIG,

37
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:48,599
highest temperature of any electric utility nuclear plant, remain essentially constant at

38
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:55,600
all loads above 25 percent of full power. During a typical three months of commercial

39
00:04:56,500 --> 00:05:01,400
operation, more than 100 million kilowatt hours of electricity were generated by the

40
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:08,400
nuclear facility, with the plant availability of over 99 percent. Fuel is transferred by

41
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:15,700
Fuel is transferred by a 250-ton handling machine.

42
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:26,120
A fuel element can be replaced without cool down in a matter of a few hours.

43
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:33,180
The reactor is presently fueled with 140 metallic uranium molybdenum elements and 10 uranium

44
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:37,700
carbide elements.

45
00:05:37,699 --> 00:05:44,199
carbide elements have been irradiated in the sodium reactor experiment and Hallam.

46
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:49,639
Indications are that uranium carbide fuel will attain long life and low fuel

47
00:05:49,639 --> 00:05:59,180
costs. The Hallam second core loading will be all uranium carbide fuel.

48
00:06:01,139 --> 00:06:05,480
Operation and maintenance of Hallam sodium systems has been simple and

49
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:13,280
straightforward. The sodium has been handled as safely and efficiently as any

50
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:21,400
common industrial liquid. The entire Hallam nuclear power facility has been

51
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:28,080
reliable and stable. As a result, more advanced sodium graphite nuclear plants

52
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:33,140
of larger capacity and higher efficiency have been designed and are ready for

53
00:06:33,139 --> 00:06:38,039
construction to assist in serving the growing power demands of the United States.
